  "title": "Door lock that opens only for codes 0, 2, 7, 8, 9, 14, built from only NAND chips, at most 16",
  "spec": "A door lock with 4 switches a, b, c, d (a is the biggest digit of the binary number): the light y turns on only when the switches show the numbers 0, 2, 7, 8, 9 or 14, and stays off for every other number. Build it using only NAND chips (a NOT is a NAND with both inputs tied together) and at most 16 chips in total.",
